==Agonymium==
{{Lore Entry
|image=ON-object-Agonymium Stone.jpg
|imgdesc=Agonymium Stone
|description=Agonymium is a type of stone that possesses the power to consume mortal misery. It is usually grey in color, but glows red when infused with the screams of mortal agony. The stone can become dormant and lose this ability.{{ref|[[Online:Agonymium Stone, Inert|Agonymium Stone, Inert]] furnishing in [[ESO:Online|ESO]]}} Concentrating on a fragment of agonymium can cause a mortal to temporarily discorporate, splitting into slivers of individualized torment.{{ref|[[Online:Agonymium Stone (memento)|Agonymium Stone]] memento in [[ESO:Online|ESO]]}} Pillars of agonymium engraved with [[Lore:Daedric Alphabet|Daedric writing]] were used extensively throughout the [[Lore:Dread Cellar|Dread Cellar]].{{ref|[[Online:Agonymium Stone (object)|Agonymium Stone]]s in [[Online:The Dread Cellar|the Dread Cellar]] in [[ESO:Online|ESO]]}}
|place=*[[Online:Agonymium Stone|ESO]]
}}

==Alabaster==
{{Lore Entry
|image=ON-concept-Gonfalon Bay.jpg
|imgdesc=Alabaster cliffs
|description='''Alabaster''' is a white stone. Cliff faces made of alabaster can be found in [[Lore:High Isle|High Isle]].{{Ref|name=HiC|[[Online:Concept Art/High Isle|High Isle Concept Art]]}}{{Ref|name=ONHCP|group=UOL|[[General:High Isle Chapter Preview|High Isle Chapter Preview]]}} The walls of the eponymous settlement of [[Lore:Alabaster|Alabaster]] are said to be made from it, as are some [[Lore:Ayleid Ruins|Ayleid ruins]].{{Ref|name=RoC|{{Cite Book|Remnants of Cyrod}}}}{{Ref|name=AC|[[ON:Ayleid Crate|Ayleid Crate]] description}} The [[Lore:Resolution of Zenithar|Resolution of Zenithar]] is in possession of a hundred-foot tall obelisk made of alabaster that stands above all as a symbol welcoming commerce, and is said to be so finely polished that it reflected back shades of the sea and sky.{{ref|name=TPPlayingHouses|group=UOL|[[General:Ted Peterson|Ted Peterson]]'s posts in [[General:Loranna's RP#Campaign 12: Playing Houses|''Playing Houses'']]}} Alabaster is a common enough material that jars made out of it were found dating from the earliest years of the Second Era.{{Ref|name=FSoBD|{{Cite Book|The First Scroll of Baan Dar}}}}
}}

