==Basalt==
{{Lore Entry
|image=ON-furnishing-Rocks, Basalt Chunks.jpg
|imgdesc=Basalt
|description='''Basalt''' is a heavy, coarse stone known to have formed in hexagonal pillars on [[Lore:Solstheim|Solstheim]].{{Ref|name=TESVSPOGG|{{Cite Book|The Elder Scrolls V: Skyrim: Prima Official Game Guide|ns_base=Books}}}}{{Ref|name=HKN|{{Cite Book|Hand Kenro's Note|ns_base=Skyrim}}}}{{ref|name=DBCK|group=UOL|EditorIDs of static objects on [[Skyrim:Solstheim|Solstheim]] in ''[[Skyrim:Skyrim|Skyrim]]''}} Basalt is often considered to be unsuitable for delicate stonework, but early [[Lore:Dunmer|Dunmer]] are known to have crafted with it regardless,{{ref|[[Online:Bal Foyen Antiquities#Basalt Table-Game Set|Basalt Table-Game Set]] Antiquity Codex entry in [[Online:Online|ESO]]: ''[[Online:Greymoor|Greymoor]]''}} particularly in the walls of buildings in [[Lore:Vivec City|Vivec City]].{{Ref|name=VP|[[:File:ON-concept-Vivec Palace 02.jpg|Vivec Palace art]]}} The [[Lore:Heartlands|Heartlands]] of [[Lore:Cyrodiil|Cyrodiil]] are noted for their basalt; basalt taken from the [[Lore:Niben River|Niben River]] is particularly sturdy.{{ref|[[ON:Ayleid Blacksmithing Station|Ayleid Blacksmithing Station]] Heartland Basalt Base Codex entry in [[ESO:Online|ESO]]}}
{{NewLeft}}
|place=*[[Skyrim:Solstheim|Skyrim]]{{DB}},{{Ref|name=TESVSPOGG}} [[Online:Conservatory Furnishings/Stones and Pebbles|ESO]]
