==Granite==
{{Lore Entry
|image=ON-furnishing-Rock, Granite Chunk.jpg
|imgdesc=Granite
|description=Granite is a type of stone. The Charred Ridge is a granite mountain range that separates [[Lore:Stonefalls|Stonefalls]] and [[Lore:Deshaan|Deshaan]]. The [[Lore:Tormented Spire|Tormented Spire]] is its highest peak and anchors it to the west.{{Ref|name=ONLoadTormented1|[[Online:Tormented Spire|Tormented Spire]] loading screen text in [[Online:Online|ESO]]}}{{Ref|name=ONLoadCharred|[[Online:Charred Ridge|Charred Ridge]] loading screen text in [[Online:Online|ESO]]}} When [[Lore:Vivec City|Vivec City]] was expanding in the mid-[[Lore:Second Era|Second Era]], a granite quarry was built in [[Lore:Foyada Mamaea|Foyada Mamaea]] and became the project's main source of granite. The operation closed when [[Lore:Red Mountain|Red Mountain]] erupted a lava flowed in through the site.{{Ref|name=ONLoadFoyada|[[Online:Foyada Quarry|Foyada Quarry]] loading screen text in [[Online:Online|ESO]]&#58; ''[[Online:Morrowind (DLC)|Morrowind]]''}}

The mines of [[Lore:Markarth|Markarth]] harvested granite and its supplies were used to build Castle [[Lore:Evermore|Evermore]]'s battlements.{{Ref|name=EGTB|{{Cite Book|EGT|Bangkorai}}}} The [[Lore:Mount Kilkreath|Mount Kilkreath]] foothills of [[Lore:Haafingar|Haafingar]] are made of granite.{{Ref|name=TESVSPOGG|{{Cite Book|The Elder Scrolls V: Skyrim: Prima Official Game Guide|ns_base=BK}}}}{{rp|415}} [[Lore:Granite Hill|Granite Hill]] is a historical settlement in [[Lore:Skyrim|Skyrim]], specifically in [[Lore:Falkreath Hold|Falkreath Hold]]. The word used for "granite" in the [[Lore:Dragon Language|dragon language]] is "Quethsegol" meaning "stone,"{{Ref|name=HOJG|{{Cite Book|Holdings of Jarl Gjalund}}}}{{Ref|name=TESVSPOGG}} or literally "[[Lore:Earthbones|Bone-of-earth]]."{{Ref|name=TESVSPOGG|{{Cite Book|The Elder Scrolls V: Skyrim: Prima Official Game Guide|ns_base=Books}}}} Previously, Nordic stonesmiths used [[Lore:Porphyry|porphyry]] deposits to erect igneous rocks for architecture, but by the [[Lore:Second Era|Second Era]], it was replaced with hard-wearing granite and volcanic stone.{{Ref|name=EGTS|{{Cite Book|EGT|Skyrim}}}}

In the middle of [[Lore:Auridon|Auridon]], just west of [[Lore:Skywatch|Skywatch]] is a large, white granite mountain.{{Ref|name=EGTA|{{Cite Book|EGT|Summerset Isles}}}} As the range travels north, it hardens and forms the jagged promontories of the north coast. Several sites of interest, like the town of [[Lore:Shattered Grove|Shattered Grove]], the temple ruins of [[Lore:Tanzelwil|Tanzelwil]], and the former royal summer home in the Glister Vale are found in its vicinity.{{Ref|name=ONAuridon|[[Online:Auridon|Auridon]] in [[Online:Online|ESO]]}} The steps of [[Lore:Ceyatatar|Ceyatatar]] in [[Lore:Cyrodiil|Cyrodiil]] are made of granite and is where [[Lore:Pelinal Whitestrake|Pelinal Whitestrake]] slew the Fire-King, [[Lore:Hadhuul|Hadhuul]].{{Ref|name=TSOP|{{Cite Book|The Song of Pelinal, v 3}}}}
|place=*[[Online:Conservatory Furnishings/Boulders and Large Rocks|ESO]]
}}

